  "summary": "The Sedro-Woolley City Council voted to reactivate its seven Flock ALPR cameras by June 1, 2026, after they were disabled in June 2025 following a public records request. The decision follows new Washington state legislation signed by Gov. Bob Ferguson restricting access to authorized law enforcement and barring federal/immigration use.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Sedro-Woolley's seven Flock cameras went live in March 2025 and were disabled in June 2025 after a public records request was filed for images taken by the cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "A new state law limits images to authorized law enforcement personnel for valid law enforcement purposes. Federal agencies are prohibited from accessing Flock camera data, including for immigration enforcement.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "I was able to negotiate with Flock and since it has been turned off for so long, to get a prorated discount on the time we lost",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
